  {
   "index": 11,
   "tag": "p×3",
   "landmarks": [
    "main",
    "section"
   ],
   "textLength": 446,
   "text": "Menopause is when you have your final period. You have reached menopause if you haven’t had a period or spotting for 12 months.\nMost women reach menopause between the ages of 45 and 55. In Australia, the average age to reach menopause is 51 to 52. \nMenopause can happen naturally at the expected age or early.\nMenopause before the age of 45 is called ‘early menopause’. If menopause happens before th",
