    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 13,
   "tag": "p×2",
   "landmarks": [
    "main",
    "section"
   ],
   "textLength": 317,
   "text": "Menopause happens because your hormone levels (e.g. oestrogen levels) drop and you stop ovulating and having periods. \nMenopause can also happen due to surgery or cancer treatment.\nAs you approach menopause, your hormones (e.g. oestrogen and progesterone) go up and down. These changes can lead to different symptoms.",
   "counts": {
